# Cloudflare's copy of vercel.json's `rewrites`: only these paths serve the app (status 200);
# every other path gets public/404.html with a 404 status (wrangler.jsonc `not_found_handling`).
# The target is `/`, not `/index.html`: Cloudflare answers /index.html with a 307 to `/`, which
# would drop the path. apps/web/src/net/cloudflare-config.test.ts holds this list equal to
# vercel.json's.
#
# A page the build writes (apps/web/static-pages.ts) is rewritten to its own folder, not to `/`: a
# rule wins over a file, and a path with no rule gets a 307 to the slashed path. Its slashed path is
# served by the file itself.

/login /login/ 200
/reset-password / 200
/reset-password/ / 200
